{
  "name": "Audio Power Amplifier (op-amp + Class-AB, 8 ohm)",
  "description": "A complete power amplifier: an op-amp gain stage driving a complementary NPN/PNP Class-AB output stage that sits INSIDE a global negative-feedback loop (closed-loop gain x5, set by Rf/Rg), feeding an 8 ohm speaker with a Zobel network for stability and an AC-coupled input. +/-15V rails. Run a transient: a 0.5V 1kHz input becomes ~2.5V at the speaker (about 0.4W), the feedback loop suppressing the output-stage crossover distortion. (Validated on ngspice: x5 gain, clean.)",
  "tags": [
    "amplifier",
    "audio",
    "class-ab",
    "power",
    "feedback",
    "flagship",
    "advanced"
  ],
